-- For each prime p, tight frames of every large length with a vector v such
-- that every s₁·conj τ(v) is a p-adic unit, s₁ the period factor; the
-- p-adic size of s₁ at each place.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Curve/TightFrameExists.lean ("This file: For
-- each prime p, tight frames of every large length with a vector v such
-- that every s₁·conj τ(v) is a p-adic unit, s₁ =
-- `Parameters.periodFactor`."; Parameters.adeleExtension_alpha,
-- norm_iota_periodFactor, norm_periodFactor_mul_conj_le_one,
-- norm_iota_periodFactor_eq_one, isTightFrame_zeta_pow,
-- exists_isTightFrame).
-- Encoding. E = fieldE(P, s) is a subfield of ℂ and the place τ its
-- embedding placeEmbeddingE(P, s, τ). The source's weightEmbedding ιₚ τ is
-- x ↦ ιₚ(τ(x̄)); the component of α along it is 1/ιₚ(τ(P′(ζ)‾)) if the
-- induced place contains (1 + √−d)/2 and 1 otherwise
-- (adeleExtension_alpha), so norm_iota_periodFactor is stated with that
-- value. "α⁻¹y integral" (finiteImage id y ∈ Ô) is IntegralAfterAlpha. Not
-- stated here: the helpers coe_trace_eq_sum, herm_mem_quadInt and
-- exists_cyclotomic_different_factor.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
